DGM: Deep Graph Clustering with MinCut for Analysis of Single-Cell Transcriptomics

This repository contains the official implementation of the paper “DGM: Deep Graph Clustering with MinCut for Analysis of Single-Cell Transcriptomics”.

1. Environment Setup

We recommend using Python 3.9.13. You can set up the environment using conda or pip.

Using Conda (Recommended)

# 1. Create and activate a new conda environment
conda create -n dgm python=3.9.13
conda activate dgm

# 2. Install PyTorch 
# For example:
pip install torch==2.0 

# 3. Install PyTorch Geometric
conda install pyg -c pyg

# 4. Install other dependencies
pip install numpy scipy scikit-learn pandas scanpy h5py


Using pip

pip install torch 
pip install torch_geometric
pip install numpy scipy scikit-learn pandas scanpy h5py


2. Data Preparation

2.1 Download Datasets

This project uses single-cell RNA-seq data in .h5 (h5ad) format. 

2.2 Organize the Directory

Place your downloaded dataset file (e.g., data.h5) into the following directory structure:

Your-Project-Root/
├── dataset/
│   └── Adam/          # Example dataset folder
│       ├── data.h5    # Raw data file
│       └── (other files will be generated by the pipeline)
├── code/               # Source code files
│   ├── preprocess.py
│   ├── autoencoder.py
│   ├── graph_construction.py
│   ├── graph_clustering.py
│   └── utils.py
└── README.md

3. Quick Start: Running the Full Pipeline

The following steps will guide you through preprocessing, feature extraction, graph construction, and clustering on the Adam dataset.

Step 1: Data Preprocessing & Feature Extraction

This step normalizes the raw data and saves the processed feature matrix and labels.
python src/preprocess.py

Outputs in dataset/Adam/:
• feature.npy: Normalized gene expression matrix.

• label.npy: Cell type labels.

Step 2: Dimensionality Reduction with Autoencoder

This step compresses the high-dimensional features into a low-dimensional latent space.
python src/autoencoder.py

Outputs in dataset/Adam/:
• features.npy: Low-dimensional features (used for graph construction).

Step 3: Graph Construction

Builds a cell-cell similarity graph (K-Nearest Neighbor graph) from the reduced features.
python code/graph_construction.py

Output in dataset/Adam/:
• edge_list.txt: The edge list of the constructed graph.

Step 4: Graph Clustering with DGM

Runs the DGM model on the constructed graph to perform cell clustering.
python code/graph_clustering.py

Output: The script prints the best ARI and NMI scores achieved during training to the console. 

4. Code Structure

• code/preprocess.py: Loads .h5 data, performs Scanpy-based normalization, filtering, and scaling.

• code/autoencoder.py: Defines and pre-trains the autoencoder for dimensionality reduction.

• code/graph_construction.py: Constructs the KNN graph using various similarity metrics (RBF, cosine, etc.).

• code/graph_clustering.py: Core implementation of the DGM model, including the higher-order MinCut loss.

• code/utils.py: Utility functions (data loading, metric calculation, adjacency matrix normalization).








